  "context": "# Goal\nTameshi round 36 (verification-fixture craft), ONE v1 wave under policy v1 (band 32-64). The L1 landed and committed everything under attack BEFORE this wave: the claims and their receipts live at the lane tip named in the dispatch message. Claims under attack: C1 (calibration; cold-read monitor refresh of the four round-35-drifted SKILL headings restores credit 6 -> 8 per `python3 /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-21/coldread/measure.py --repo /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin --rev REV`) and C2 (depth surface; successor counter `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-36/c1/c1-measure-v2.py` adds frozen public-slot cardinality + distinctness asserts 6/3/9 over the round-35 tally-audit panel). Contract: `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-36/contract.json`. The L1 holds the canonical planner seat (orchestrator ruling 2026-10-19: planner is a frozen-topology seat, never a swarm role); a bounded planning data-walk rides this wave's scout/connector items.\n\n# Frozen artifacts (NEVER edit; read-only)\n- `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/tools/tally-audit-v3.py` sha256 6188db16de045f2927df2a0e667bc1539f4acfce5a1ac116e6de3107bf15d354\n- `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/tools/mutate-and-run.sh` sha256 a7d3f2dd7d47511a4769aab610dd85d1a37e77b32f14fd763f3af638dd912eb9 (byte-pinned, NEVER edited)\n- `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-35/c1/c1-measure.py` (v1 counter, frozen) and `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-36/c1/c1-measure-v2.py` sha256 9eb8944c25414da11400dce92afaf047c4874b6bd800bfe15219572e9da8fa53 (frozen v2 successor)\n- `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-21/coldread/ledger.json` (the cold-read ledger the refresh appended four entries to)\n\n# Bounds (hard)\n- Your tools start at the FLEET ROOT. Every path you use MUST be absolute; a relative path such as `.ufo/waves/...` lands in the FLEET repo and is a scope violation. Every `Report:` trailer the dispatcher prints is relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin — write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/<that path>, which is the ONLY lane path you may create.\n- NEVER write inside any git checkout's `.git`, never run a mutating jj or git command, never edit the lane, the fleet repo, sibling lanes, `.ufo/state/`, or any file under /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/ except your own report. All scratch work goes under /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r36-seats/<YourName>/.\n- Do not run `pacman` at all (host transactions are paused). Tooling directive (operator 2026-10-19): you may install or upgrade tools that help the task without asking, via `uv tool install`, `npx`, or an official release binary into `~/.local/bin` — official sources only, never piped remote scripts; record tool/version/channel/reason in your report.\n- Seats are leaf seats: do not spawn subagents. Read-only seats return findings without production edits.\n\n# Report\nWrite your report at the `Report:` path named in your dispatch trailer (relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin). It must name what you attacked, the exact commands run (with revisions), and a verdict line.\n",
